 {"id":"QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-12","title":"[P2] test_snapshot_saved_to_file fails on the fresh agent in BOTH cap arms while green on dev box and fresh venv \u2014 _log_state_snapshot swallows write errors and the test asserts file existence, so any env write failure grades as an opaque test failure","priority":"P2","status":"pending","worker_status":"pending","reasoning":"QA foreman cycle 2026-09-29 (same battery as QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-11). Native suite: 'FAILED tests/test_failsafe.py::TestEmergencyRecovery::test_snapshot_saved_to_file' stopping after 1 failure (1 failed, 1441 passed, 2 skipped, 76s) under the 3G cap AND act-arm context shows the same test name failing uncapped. Controls: dev box .venv single-test PASS (also after rm -rf /tmp/test_snapshots); fresh py3.12 venv FULL suite 4310 passed, 14 skipped, 0 failed (254s). Code reading: src/core/failsafe.py _log_state_snapshot wraps the snapshot write in try/except and only appends 'snapshot_failed: <e>' to its actions list \u2014 the error never propagates \u2014 while tests/test_failsafe.py:515 asserts os.listdir shows a snapshot_* file. Any environmental write failure (fs, permissions, disk) therefore surfaces as a bare assertion failure with the real cause swallowed. Additional brittleness: the test writes to the SHARED, HARDCODED /tmp/test_snapshots and after asserting deletes only snapshot_* files \u2014 verified residue leak: emergency_report_*.json survives every passing run and is visible to sibling runs on a multi-tenant machine. Candidate agent-side trigger: /tmp contention or ALC/overlay fs behavior on the agent; exact agent-side exception unprovable post-hoc (logs died with the agent) \u2014 the swallowed-exception mechanism is verified from source.","review_notes":"Repro: fresh agent + battery (evidence jsonl chaos-resource cell has the failure tail). Local controls: .venv/bin/pytest 'tests/test_failsafe.py::TestEmergencyRecovery::test_snapshot_saved_to_file' -q = 1 passed; fresh venv full suite 4310 passed. Fix direction (product): (a) let _log_state_snapshot's write failure propagate or have the test assert on 'snapshot_saved:' in result actions so the real error surfaces; (b) test should use tmp_path fixture, not shared /tmp/test_snapshots; (c) cleanup should remove emergency_report_* too (verified leak: the file survives a passing run). chaos-resource FAIL this cycle is the SAME defect cascaded under the cap, not an independent memory finding (contrast 09-27's cascaded cap verdict in QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-10).","worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":null,"complexity":2,"capability_tags":["qa","ci","test-robustness"],"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"dispatched_at":null,"completed_at":null,"attempts":0,"exit_code":null,"commit_hash":null,"files_changed":[],"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"blocked_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:00+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:00+00:00","worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"acceptance_criteria":"(M) fresh clone status is clean with respect to .coding-hermes/board/: board.parquet either listed in .gitignore or removed; `git status --short .coding-hermes/board/` shows no untracked entries after a normal tick."}
